 "id": "torque-standard",
 "title": "Standard tightening torques by size, finish and grade",
 "use": "For a fastener with no value from Porsche. The torque book names such rows \"Torque Value Table\". Read the grade (8.8, 10.9, 12.9) stamped on the bolt head and the colour of the finish: yellow = ZN, silver = ZNS. Only then take the value.",
 "rules": [
  "Porsche models may use fasteners that can only be tightened once. When these fasteners are removed or loosened, discard and replace with new parts.",
  "These are standard tightening torques and do not apply to torque-to-yield fasteners.",
  "The torque values apply to the noted fastener finish only: yellow (ZN) or silver (ZNS).",
  "Not applicable when using a different surface or lubricant on the thread, or if the height of the nut differs.",
  "Not applicable to necked-down bolts, self-tapping screw connections or to connections between parts made of different materials."
 ],
